# PROJECT TITLE
Juaboso Government Hospital — Smart Bed Management, Ward Coordination and Hospital Operations Dashboard

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Build a modern, secure, fully functional, responsive, web-based Hospital Bed Management and Ward Coordination System for Juaboso Government Hospital in the Western North Region of Ghana.

The system will serve as a centralized digital platform connecting hospital management, ward managers, nurses, doctors, admission officers, emergency department staff, records officers, and other authorized healthcare personnel.

The primary objective is to enable hospital management to know, at any time:

- The total number of beds available across the hospital.
- The number of occupied, available, reserved, blocked, and out-of-service beds.
- Which wards are approaching full capacity or are already full.
- Which departments urgently require additional beds.
- Which wards have patients awaiting admission, discharge, or transfer.
- Which wards have pending bed requests.
- Where patients are being transferred from and where they are going.
- Which departments need additional operational support.
- What is happening across all wards without physically visiting each department.
- How bed occupancy and demand change throughout the day, week, and month.

The platform must provide live operational updates, centralized reporting, notifications, audit trails, and role-based access.

This must be a working full-stack application, not merely a dashboard mockup or static design.

All buttons, forms, filters, charts, tables, status changes, notifications, and user actions must work and be connected to the underlying database.

Do not present fabricated operational information as actual hospital data. Use clearly labeled demonstration data during development and allow authorized administrators to replace it with verified hospital information.

