## 13. USER ROLES AND ACCESS CONTROL

Implement role-based access control.

### Role 1: System Administrator

Permissions:

- Manage user accounts.
- Assign roles.
- Configure hospital settings.
- Create and edit wards.
- Configure bed categories.
- Register beds.
- Manage operational thresholds.
- Configure notification rules.
- Review system health.
- Review audit logs.
- Manage integrations.

System administrators should not automatically receive unrestricted access to clinical records simply because they administer the software.

### Role 2: Hospital Management

Permissions:

- View the hospital-wide dashboard.
- Monitor occupancy across all wards.
- View operational alerts.
- Review bed demand.
- Monitor transfers.
- View authorized reports.
- Review unresolved operational issues.
- Approve specified capacity requests.
- Track department performance.

Patient-level access should be limited to the minimum information needed for authorized operational duties.

### Role 3: Ward Manager

Permissions:

- View the assigned ward.
- View and manage its bed inventory.
- Review admissions and transfers.
- Submit bed requests.
- Report operational problems.
- Coordinate cleaning and readiness.
- Assign permitted ward tasks.
- View ward-level reports.
- Receive and respond to relevant notifications.

### Role 4: Nurse or Authorized Ward Staff

Permissions:

- View relevant ward bed status.
- Record permitted bed status changes.
- Update assigned operational tasks.
- Submit ward reports.
- Coordinate approved admissions and transfers.
- Acknowledge relevant alerts.

Access to clinical information must follow separately configured permissions.

### Role 5: Admission Officer

Permissions:

- Create and review admission coordination records.
- Submit bed requests.
- View permitted bed availability.
- Track approved allocations.
- Coordinate admission workflows.

### Role 6: Doctor or Authorized Clinical Officer

Permissions:

- Access clinical functions specifically authorized for the role.
- Submit or review admission and transfer requests.
- Record permitted clinical decisions.
- View necessary patient information.

### Role 7: Cleaning and Maintenance Staff

Permissions:

- View assigned cleaning or maintenance tasks.
- Update task status.
- Record task completion.
- Report problems preventing a bed from returning to service.

These users must not have unrestricted access to patient records.

### Role 8: Read-Only Auditor

Permissions:

- View approved reports.
- Review authorized audit events.
- Export permitted operational data.

No permission to alter patient assignments or operational records.

### Security requirements

- Deny access by default.
- Enforce permissions on the backend, not only in the user interface.
- Validate every sensitive action.
- Restrict ward-specific access where appropriate.
- Require authorized approval for high-impact actions.
- Keep a complete audit trail.
- Terminate or expire inactive sessions according to policy.
- Prevent users from granting themselves additional permissions.

