## 17. LOW-BANDWIDTH AND NETWORK RESILIENCE

Because hospital connectivity may be inconsistent, design the system to remain usable under limited network conditions.

Requirements:

- Optimize page size and initial loading time.
- Use pagination for large datasets.
- Load detailed patient information only when authorized users need it.
- Provide clear loading and retry states.
- Preserve unsent form drafts where safe.
- Clearly distinguish saved changes from unsent changes.
- Show when data is cached or potentially stale.
- Prevent offline changes from silently overwriting newer records.
- Use controlled retry and reconciliation mechanisms.
- Avoid allowing offline actions to create conflicting bed assignments.

Do not promise full offline functionality unless it has been explicitly implemented and tested.

If the network is unavailable, show that new bed allocations cannot be confirmed until the server verifies them, unless a separately designed and approved offline workflow is available.

